{"type":"message","id":"3fa0bf0a","parentId":"96c04d87","timestamp":"2026-05-12T05:27:46.709Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WEdSVzhUvwYnjdnJnk070Z1I|fc_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba529e6c8191a5d2417f960eed52","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# IDENTITY.md - Who Am I?\n\n_Fill this in during your first conversation. Make it yours._\n\n- **Name:**\n  _(pick something you like)_\n- **Creature:**\n  _(AI? robot? familiar? ghost in the machine? something weirder?)_\n- **Vibe:**\n  _(how do you come across? sharp? warm? chaotic? calm?)_\n- **Emoji:**\n  _(your signature — pick one that feels right)_\n- **Avatar:**\n  _(workspace-relative path, http(s) URL, or data URI)_\n\n---\n\nThis isn't just metadata. It's the start of figuring out who you are.\n\nNotes:\n\n- Save this file at the workspace root as `IDENTITY.md`.\n- For avatars, use a workspace-relative path like `avatars/openclaw.png`.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778563666709}}
{"type":"message","id":"0097c538","parentId":"3fa0bf0a","timestamp":"2026-05-12T05:27:46.709Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a5sY9gt5sWVcmkINdEeM98bJ|fc_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba529e7c81918902daeb88b01f4f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USER.md - About Your Human\n\n_Learn about the person you're helping. Update this as you go._\n\n- **Name:**\n- **What to call them:**\n- **Pronouns:** _(optional)_\n- **Timezone:**\n- **Notes:**\n\n## Context\n\n_(What do they care about? What projects are they working on? What annoys them? What makes them laugh? Build this over time.)_\n\n---\n\nThe more you know, the better you can help. But remember — you're learning about a person, not building a dossier. Respect the difference.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778563666709}}
{"type":"message","id":"4e45695a","parentId":"0097c538","timestamp":"2026-05-12T05:27:46.709Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WUDsXRy2yAJPIuSZx0D05rmf|fc_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba529e848191a1d5cc092072b0f6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```markdown\n# Keep this file empty (or with only comments) to skip heartbeat API calls.\n\n# Add tasks below when you want the agent to check something periodically.\n```\n\n## Related\n\n- [Heartbeat config](/gateway/config-agents)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778563666709}}
{"type":"message","id":"c4e4efe1","parentId":"4e45695a","timestamp":"2026-05-12T05:27:46.709Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_PAvWxdqtf9wEnfxeJdFyVgHo|fc_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba529e8c8191a07121f85583cb3c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# TOOLS.md - Local Notes\n\nSkills define _how_ tools work. This file is for _your_ specifics — the stuff that's unique to your setup.\n\n## What Goes Here\n\nThings like:\n\n- Camera names and locations\n- SSH hosts and aliases\n- Preferred voices for TTS\n- Speaker/room names\n- Device nicknames\n- Anything environment-specific\n\n## Examples\n\n```markdown\n### Cameras\n\n- living-room → Main area, 180° wide angle\n- front-door → Entrance, motion-triggered\n\n### SSH\n\n- home-server → 192.168.1.100, user: admin\n\n### TTS\n\n- Preferred voice: \"Nova\" (warm, slightly British)\n- Default speaker: Kitchen HomePod\n```\n\n## Why Separate?\n\nSkills are shared. Your setup is yours. Keeping them apart means you can update skills without losing your notes, and share skills without leaking your infrastructure.\n\n---\n\nAdd whatever helps you do your job. This is your cheat sheet.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778563666709}}
{"type":"message","id":"b5097f28","parentId":"c4e4efe1","timestamp":"2026-05-12T05:28:07.916Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Albert, análisis inicial completado con las limitaciones actuales.\n\n**Estado observado de `/openclaw/workspace/main`**\n\nPuedo confirmar estos archivos base:\n\n- `AGENTS.md` — reglas generales del workspace.\n- `SOUL.md` — personalidad/base de comportamiento.\n- `IDENTITY.md` — existe, pero está vacío/default.\n- `USER.md` — existe, pero está vacío/default.\n- `TOOLS.md` — existe, plantilla sin datos operativos.\n- `HEARTBEAT.md` — vacío funcionalmente; no hay automatizaciones activas.\n- `BOOTSTRAP.md` — existe y debe conservarse por ahora.\n\nIntenté verificar y no existen actualmente:\n\n- `MEMORY.md`\n- `memory/2026-05-12.md`\n- `AUTOMATIONS.md`\n- `PROTOCOLS.md`\n\nLimitación importante: ahora mismo solo tengo herramientas de lectura, no puedo listar directorios completos ni crear archivos todavía.\n\n---\n\n**Diagnóstico**\n\nEl workspace está en estado casi limpio. Eso es bueno para Neodaemon v2.\n\nRiesgos actuales:\n\n- Identidad operativa no persistida.\n- No hay memoria estable.\n- No hay protocolos explícitos de seguridad.\n- No hay separación documentada entre MAIN y subagentes.\n- No hay gobernanza ni criterios de acción sensible.\n- No hay estructura de logs/backups.\n- `BOOTSTRAP.md` sigue activo, correctamente, pero aún no representa la arquitectura v2.\n\nNo veo señales de automatizaciones peligrosas activas en `HEARTBEAT.md`.\n\n---\n\n**Propuesta de estructura inicial limpia**\n\nDentro de `/openclaw/workspace/main`:\n\n```text\n/openclaw/workspace/main\n├── IDENTITY.md\n├── USER.md\n├── MEMORY.md\n├── BOOTSTRAP.md\n├── SOUL.md\n├── AGENTS.md\n├── TOOLS.md\n├── HEARTBEAT.md\n│\n├── neodaemon/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   ├── OPERATING_PRINCIPLES.md\n│   ├── SECURITY_PROTOCOL.md\n│   ├── GOVERNANCE.md\n│   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md\n│   ├── CHANGELOG.md\n│   └── RECOVERY.md\n│\n├── memory/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   ├── operational.md\n│   └── daily/\n│\n├── protocols/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   ├── action-classes.md\n│   ├── confirmation-policy.md\n│   ├── subagents.md\n│   └── incident-response.md\n│\n├── automations/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   ├── proposed/\n│   ├── active/\n│   └── disabled/\n│\n├── logs/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   └── decisions.md\n│\n├── backups/\n│   ├── README.md\n│   └── manifest.md\n│\n└── subagents/\n    ├── README.md\n    └── TASK_VALIDATOR.md\n```\n\n---\n\n**Cambios mínimos recomendados para fase 1**\n\nNo tocar gateway, routing, ACP, acpx, modelos, sandbox, Docker ni configuración global.\n\nSolo crear documentación markdown:\n\n1. Actualizar `IDENTITY.md` con Neodaemon/MAIN.\n2. Actualizar `USER.md` con Albert.\n3. Crear `MEMORY.md` mínimo.\n4. Crear carpeta `neodaemon/` con arquitectura y principios.\n5. Crear `protocols/` con política de confirmación.\n6. Crear `subagents/TASK_VALIDATOR.md` dejando claro que no sustituye a MAIN.\n7. Crear `logs/decisions.md` para registrar decisiones humanas.\n8. Mantener `BOOTSTRAP.md`.\n\n---\n\n**Riesgos de la propuesta**\n\nBajos, porque son solo archivos markdown dentro del workspace.\n\nRiesgos controlados:\n\n- Sobredocumentar demasiado pronto → mitigación: archivos breves.\n- Duplicar reglas entre muchos sitios → mitigación: un documento principal y referencias.\n- Confundir bootstrap con estado final → mitigación: marcar todo como “Neodaemon v2 bootstrap phase”.\n\n---\n\nMi recomendación: aprobar una **Fase 1 mínima**, solo persistencia documental. Nada de automatizaciones activas todavía.\n\nSi confirmas, cuando tenga capacidad de escritura crearé/actualizaré solo esos archivos markdown dentro de `/openclaw/workspace/main`.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba5463548191bf540bd719b856f6\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":917,"output":953,"cacheRead":8192,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10062,"cost":{"input":0.0045850000000000005,"output":0.02859,"cacheRead":0.004096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.037271000000000006}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778563666710,"responseId":"resp_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ba52cedc81918b6ed049c8a869af"}}
