{"type":"message","id":"b87536dc","parentId":"f422ac60","timestamp":"2026-05-12T08:53:12.793Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cziRGAzb8EoRMKRaqhxHN14s|fc_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ea77a55c819193a55e4dfea520e0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# backup-ligero-operativo-v2.sh\n# Estado: PROPUESTA, NO EJECUTAR SIN CONFIRMACIÓN HUMANA\n# Default: dry-run. Real execution requires explicit --execute.\n\nROOT=\"/openclaw/workspace/main\"\nBACKUP_ROOT=\"$ROOT/backups/operational\"\nMODE=\"dry-run\"\n\nusage() {\n  cat <<'USAGE'\nUsage:\n  backup-ligero-operativo-v2.sh [--dry-run]\n  backup-ligero-operativo-v2.sh --execute\n\nDefault mode is --dry-run.\n\nThis script is limited to /openclaw/workspace/main and writes backups only to:\n  /openclaw/workspace/main/backups/operational\n\nIt does not touch gateway, global config, ~/.openclaw, routing, Telegram, Docker, sandbox, models or ACP/acpx.\nUSAGE\n}\n\nfor arg in \"${@:-}\"; do\n  case \"$arg\" in\n    --dry-run)\n      MODE=\"dry-run\"\n      ;;\n    --execute)\n      MODE=\"execute\"\n      ;;\n    -h|--help)\n      usage\n      exit 0\n      ;;\n    *)\n      echo \"ERROR: unknown argument: $arg\" >&2\n      usage >&2\n      exit 2\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\nNOW_UTC=\"$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%SZ)\"\nDAY_PATH=\"$(TZ=Europe/Madrid date +%Y/%m/%d)\"\nNAME=\"${NOW_UTC}-neodaemon-main-operational-light-v2\"\nOUT_DIR=\"$BACKUP_ROOT/$DAY_PATH\"\nWORK_DIR=\"$OUT_DIR/$NAME\"\nPAYLOAD_DIR=\"$WORK_DIR/payload\"\nMANIFEST=\"$WORK_DIR/manifest.json\"\nINCLUDED_LIST=\"$WORK_DIR/included-files.txt\"\nFILE_SHA_LIST=\"$WORK_DIR/file-sha256.txt\"\nARCHIVE=\"$OUT_DIR/${NAME}.tar.gz\"\nSHA_FILE=\"$ARCHIVE.sha256\"\n\n# Safety: ensure fixed root is exactly the intended workspace.\nif [[ \"$ROOT\" != \"/openclaw/workspace/main\" ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: ROOT is not the approved workspace: $ROOT\" >&2\n  exit 3\nfi\n\nif [[ ! -d \"$ROOT\" ]]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: ROOT does not exist: $ROOT\" >&2\n  exit 3\nfi\n\n# Include only documentation/operational files from main workspace.\n# Deliberately excludes /openclaw/workspace/personal and anything outside ROOT.\nINCLUDE_PATHS=(\n  \"AGENTS.md\"\n  \"SOUL.md\"\n  \"IDENTITY.md\"\n  \"USER.md\"\n  \"TOOLS.md\"\n  \"MEMORY.md\"\n  \"HEARTBEAT.md\"\n  \"neodaemon\"\n  \"protocols\"\n  \"subagents\"\n  \"logs\"\n  \"restore\"\n  \"automations\"\n  \"backups/manifest.md\"\n  \"backups/KNOWN_SNAPSHOTS.md\"\n)\n\n# Exclusion patterns. These are applied before copy.\n# Note: name-based filtering reduces risk but does not prove absence of secrets.\nEXCLUDE_FIND_EXPR=(\n  -name '.env'\n  -o -iname '*token*'\n  -o -iname '*secret*'\n  -o -iname '*credential*'\n  -o -iname '*auth*'\n  -o -iname '*session*'\n  -o -iname '*sessions*'\n  -o -iname '*cookie*'\n  -o -iname '*cookies*'\n  -o -iname '*.pem'\n  -o -iname '*.key'\n  -o -iname '*.sqlite'\n  -o -iname '*.db'\n)\n\nis_excluded_name() {\n  local base\n  base=\"$(basename \"$1\")\"\n  shopt -s nocasematch\n  case \"$base\" in\n    .env|*token*|*secret*|*credential*|*auth*|*session*|*sessions*|*cookie*|*cookies*|*.pem|*.key|*.sqlite|*.db)\n      shopt -u nocasematch\n      return 0\n      ;;\n    *)\n      shopt -u nocasematch\n      return 1\n      ;;\n  esac\n}\n\ncollect_files() {\n  cd \"$ROOT\"\n  : > \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n\n  for item in \"${INCLUDE_PATHS[@]}\"; do\n    [[ -e \"$item\" ]] || continue\n\n    if is_excluded_name \"$item\"; then\n      continue\n    fi\n\n    if [[ -f \"$item\" ]]; then\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$item\" >> \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n    elif [[ -d \"$item\" ]]; then\n      find \"$item\" -type f \\\n        ! \\( \"${EXCLUDE_FIND_EXPR[@]}\" \\) \\\n        ! -path 'backups/operational/*' \\\n        | LC_ALL=C sort >> \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n    fi\n  done\n\n  LC_ALL=C sort -u \"$INCLUDED_LIST\" -o \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n}\n\nif [[ \"$MODE\" == \"dry-run\" ]]; then\n  TMP_BASE=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n  trap 'rm -rf \"$TMP_BASE\"' EXIT\n  WORK_DIR=\"$TMP_BASE/$NAME\"\n  PAYLOAD_DIR=\"$WORK_DIR/payload\"\n  MANIFEST=\"$WORK_DIR/manifest.json\"\n  INCLUDED_LIST=\"$WORK_DIR/included-files.txt\"\n  FILE_SHA_LIST=\"$WORK_DIR/file-sha256.txt\"\n  mkdir -p \"$WORK_DIR\"\nelse\n  mkdir -p \"$PAYLOAD_DIR\"\nfi\n\ncollect_files\n\nif [[ \"$MODE\" == \"dry-run\" ]]; then\n  cat <<EOF\nDRY-RUN ONLY. No backup archive created.\nRoot: $ROOT\nBackup target if executed: $ARCHIVE\nIncluded files list generated temporarily at: $INCLUDED_LIST\nEOF\n  cat \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\n# Execution path: copy exact included list preserving relative paths.\ncd \"$ROOT\"\nwhile IFS= read -r src; do\n  [[ -n \"$src\" ]] || continue\n  dest=\"$PAYLOAD_DIR/$src\"\n  mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$dest\")\"\n  cp -p \"$src\" \"$dest\"\ndone < \"$INCLUDED_LIST\"\n\n# Generate per-file checksums for payload contents.\n(\n  cd \"$PAYLOAD_DIR\"\n  while IFS= read -r rel; do\n    [[ -f \"$rel\" ]] || continue\n    sha256sum \"$rel\"\n  done < \"$INCLUDED_LIST\" | LC_ALL=C sort\n) > \"$FILE_SHA_LIST\"\n\ncat > \"$MANIFEST\" <<JSON\n{\n  \"created_at_utc\": \"$NOW_UTC\",\n  \"type\": \"operational_light_v2\",\n  \"mode\": \"$MODE\",\n  \"root\": \"$ROOT\",\n  \"backup_root\": \"$BACKUP_ROOT\",\n  \"archive\": \"$ARCHIVE\",\n  \"included_list\": \"included-files.txt\",\n  \"file_sha256_list\": \"file-sha256.txt\",\n  \"excludes\": [\n    \".env\",\n    \"*token*\",\n    \"*secret*\",\n    \"*credential*\",\n    \"*auth*\",\n    \"*session*\",\n    \"*sessions*\",\n    \"*cookie*\",\n    \"*cookies*\",\n    \"*.pem\",\n    \"*.key\",\n    \"*.sqlite\",\n    \"*.db\",\n    \"/openclaw/workspace/personal\",\n    \"~/.openclaw\",\n    \"gateway/global config/routing/runtime state\"\n  ],\n  \"policy\": \"Documentation-only operational light backup from /openclaw/workspace/main. No personal workspace, no global config, no runtime state. Execution requires explicit --execute and human confirmation.\"\n}\nJSON\n\n# Create archive and global checksum. No automatic retention deletion.\ntar -C \"$OUT_DIR\" -czf \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$NAME\"\nsha256sum \"$ARCHIVE\" > \"$SHA_FILE\"\n\ntar -tzf \"$ARCHIVE\" >/dev/null\nsha256sum -c \"$SHA_FILE\" >/dev/null\n\n# Remove temporary work directory after archive creation.\nrm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"\n\necho \"OK: $ARCHIVE\"\ncat \"$SHA_FILE\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778575992793}}
{"type":"message","id":"cf3d5fd2","parentId":"b87536dc","timestamp":"2026-05-12T08:53:55.261Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating file collection logic**\n\nI'm looking into a bug with the collect_files function and how the find expression works. It seems that using ! \\( expr \\) could be a problem with the array starting with -name '.env' and other options. The exclusion applies to file basenames, but I need to be cautious about including backups and logs. If logs mistakenly contain sensitive content, I’ll need human confirmation before proceeding. It's important to sort these issues out!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02ea83b0708191b686f153d0129d8f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAuqXb2hCQr54_QRurCntW3QxTLQIDphYMWwmujjGXSeHOzg1vMrOifl72vV4QQOYo44AIoaY6p85VnQfQuRtgQS4LbU8TfI1rLO14AasxY6jxILiq_rUji02t1B_gKqATN7-4QDJAt2eYhRRjckDZY4CKr-gmFcNIdyRp69rbKR5YxPWFuFtTGTkA8GoVC5pO2jJklEwCegGnk_cubCN12Rp3nt0fy1B9dvTRIpIfgAhBGJMR9-9tGW4GyO7uFpyT5dlspN6bgdJrbWxUWNiTAPhRQDL0IUR6vXffZ0r48HgiLUezjk9zQDMWmrkG7SSSZRE9b62eMqotIP1SPDgwFS_ALRZIWSvAyAfS52z-GegT94MVjSBKKG5kjZuiUfhfFekSS25bsI5sTDo73MIFqas-9IAtVfUqrmyDilJbdUL2EhQr5Odyo5bpsgqyxMd1Wt3AxIj08gp9Wos91spLTPhVpj9U97WJKHgxM0_uKcOhZMfaPSLxOAQpHKfRDcgdmA6dKjHpu_isu3Ld5Y2JHef4mxT32hXfQKRTKcF5W9HYdirm0VzSrNtJi3huQfUzT_cA2j00mbdB9lIRGfLKb567OGqinsb-Hmgi9V9rTCAL5egZQslPRcgnOdY6_wOHYHjoNyWyILhc5s-4N9vXpHWZRZ7TOhpTiAqztzHPrgzIMIN58SgDXJTkoqKnvGryrJfGsN_Nxxt2ROYOHtrUH_wgkbJzfDjoF0IIe7ZCbZw7i5xmdu5uHi_T8enLvh92TN6NrGuR06paqCn8J4O5zDStWpMno6JRAFOc053u2DaVbUItyIC11VTGNegV_vZqHAvRA3wPxG4SgshZFpWqW12hzY3Zlq_ZVq6twelVcZVZttPhwIYrS_izQQo254y6eo0wq1YDVVqaolbP1x8RXruFuOSlWW8Y-90Od8UV_H_qgwcxwh_pmXxHdL8hMoizGPCXF1YUeDfO8YwLmA_47YjFcqQW-EWqFOb-PP_XjDqT5Ml02BWj9hmmetikGhNHlk4phex3WxDZQTPdtDfUz8ZnJKeZvpFzB_ciykB6QK7nozPHkQ1G4T7-VbISVHgYvsJ8mUR_MqD08gYK7vPqaDXjsUW9VjFuo9QWZkFASMQvbA--Xtet0LtyKgYZ58PEYYjTpcryvL5JpyiKrw_Ec5JSfyZtzS8hhxMh8pc4Hm6lm97NqxIrOZ06