{"type":"message","id":"d8683213","parentId":"cbf90908","timestamp":"2026-05-12T08:56:30.194Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering file access**\n\nI’m thinking about whether I can perform a static dry-run approximation. It seems tricky because without directory listing, it’s impossible to list files. I can read specific files if I know what they are, but I can’t access the whole tree. I need to figure out an effective way to keep things concise while navigating this limitation. There's a lot to consider here!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_091df84b2f0fbfe5016a02eb27a0208191af0860b048d2fb62\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAusyu-QouAYczyfXukcyn-tM-fqxWpHqsGmudSXysIx4aZ_v-Dcy62FIBcQqEVf-74oDv-1IAK9CAy1_nINzrzdDUFGusq3agJbkih9_OCx7y_byL2_BsZuW_Pk7m0MaweR309DsFfWCRj7-LG8X4gAXbJV0GvmvIkkfyWZ89vrPA1ftQ0KzBPKbut8QdSADagRViHChTO8JjcGufYzgEE30ghXXNEI-d9SnuUPhh0X0dyzaiujzh7UejwC4Ulgh93rrMICXiwVQh27c7Zby6Hebl4jLVWdmMnVC17ekkbPQYQawHzMmJA-t0639wSf9YBV2WoZH8y3-rTj-dkHTGmAwfUrGGtx14qAqUUQSBfbM7nGVHj_Jk_5fnLiiJRt6IFo3K-Htaqt0ZKuFNb8sNyRUSwcooA269NacwKjNPjROIFlDMEXcY-wckEvldvIW56t4AQBogaBoMKd85MS-tg9KYz5-UtE_oI43o27VhPHll4oXYaa-Ird4W4TiYqfISsNBjLTmYPL9NCcGtyoCIqGEmbwcvYOs52ZfVDbStY_VXYxvjrVydGB_X-OwOBM7bM-JU8xUCC_MTnxiuJwHKMrJao5WBSWjqMYvU-s0D1fqBly0peggerKdP5fXFZaqPH9ZiUloqeekYqlt8gXXva5IPVjhSugz54mvJx2nSHDJJv02DI_b7Rq2oPUYWgsd7fefAzgu93PqZpKhkKvOpSlsGBue4q9Jcs1ep8gcterpWjxzjC12jW3cJ1tDtVz5hY4YGUWdTbBcJnNmFC-Wbe0JLrdzPddTjE47O1nOdYzwRSkxyS_xFGhCMEfo1A-NuyAtNtn2y5nRc9TcmQKpkXSvt0Qq-IOC8_H53UuEp-MzMlEBJcaNdBOISEoRvyyACYvidsdGH2mF4jUroeKovR-teaWXEwPhXr0SnwoYAMfxu2IXNx0NagbWuRsGxO5Z_7YQ_kqkdUkpqxxGaWR67yq3JUtNzfOn7lxHaCrq-makFoZwh_e4h_6IGoc7K5IfH7PSIfaBwcGsuif_4WIzYSrVE1Iyllkr9mix9883hQYjzYW5lvF5zkLlIkJulKW7FFc4_UYxGoc1u0C9vjEy3iJZtD58799OeX3MD-2TiHjM1D5GtElaU4R9NVnx59xa-ZH3b6EX58Pm5p-wkLtHhZ_bq4_p-UYiyIZbEfVY1qhTws9GXC7q93oDbGXMo2ku7BpRJA6aZUYeYWAMcEbhmy9Net-WUG-LT13Wbp48n5L3B9UtNn6ozNMmeZNzrk2KkAlJzfRTYi4