{"type":"message","id":"8fa967aa","parentId":"a47a429a","timestamp":"2026-05-12T17:50:41.900Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf (application/pdf) | /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf]\n[Telegram OpenClaw Bunker id:8785888003 Tue 2026-05-12 19:48 GMT+2] <media:document>\n\n<file name=\"DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf\" mime=\"application/pdf\">\n\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38964d74b4c92aa3\">>>\nSource: External\n---\nBest Practices for Writing & Optimizing Best Practices for Writing & Optimizing DAX DAX Efficient, Scalable, and Readable Measures  Pankaj Namekar – 6x Microsoft Certified | DM to Learn Power BI\n\nWhy DAX Best Practices Matter  Why It Matters Optimized performance = faster reports Clean code = easier maintenance Proper structure = scalable models Right techniques = accurate results  Key Goals  Accuracy Correct calculations  Performance Fast execution  Scalability Growth potential  Maintainability Easy updates Performance Impact of DAX Optimization  Optimized DAX  Reduced Overhead\n\n1 ⭐ Key Benefits  Reduces model size Measures don't consume storage space  Improves performance Calculated at query time, not refresh  Context-aware Adapts to filters and slicers  Faster refresh Less data to process during refresh  Lower memory usage Values computed when needed  Explanation  Measures calculated on query time  Calculated columns stored in model  Measures adapt to filter context  Calculated columns computed during refresh  Measure Sales Amount = SUM(Sales[SalesValue])  Calculated Column Sales[Sales Amount] = Sales[Quantity] * Sales[Price] USE MEASURES, NOT CALCULATED COLUMNS\n\n2  Modular Measures ↓ ⭐ Key Benefits  Improves readability Easier to understand complex logic  Easier debugging Isolate issues to specific measures  Reusability Use same measure in multiple calculations  Maintainability Update logic in one place  Team collaboration Easier for multiple developers  Explanation  Break complex formulas into smaller measures  Reuse measures instead of duplicating code  Create building blocks for complex calculations  Simplify maintenance and debugging process Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount]) Module 1 Total Cost = SUM(Sales[Cost]) Module 2 Total Units = SUM(Sales[Quantity]) Module 3 Profit = [Total Sales] - [Total Cost] Result  Modular Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount]) Total Cost = SUM(Sales[Cost]) Profit = [Total Sales] - [Total Cost]  Monolithic Profit = SUM(Sales[Amount]) - SUM(Sales[Cost]) KEEP DAX SIMPLE & MODULAR\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38964d74b4c92aa3\">>>\n</file>"}],"timestamp":1778608241897}}
{"type":"custom_message","customType":"openclaw.runtime-context","content":"[media attached: /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf (application/pdf) | /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Absolute and ~ paths only work when they stay inside your allowed file-read boundary; host file:// URLs are blocked. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:8785888003\",\n  \"message_id\": \"1266\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"sender\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-05-12 19:48 GMT+2\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw Bunker (8785888003)\",\n  \"id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"name\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\"\n}\n```\n\n[Telegram OpenClaw Bunker id:8785888003 Tue 2026-05-12 19:48 GMT+2] <media:document>\n\n<file name=\"DAX_Optimization---bb8e9441-3967-4c66-91cc-e6a076ebbae4.pdf\" mime=\"application/pdf\">\n\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38964d74b4c92aa3\">>>\nSource: External\n---\nBest Practices for Writing & Optimizing Best Practices for Writing & Optimizing DAX DAX Efficient, Scalable, and Readable Measures  Pankaj Namekar – 6x Microsoft Certified | DM to Learn Power BI\n\nWhy DAX Best Practices Matter  Why It Matters Optimized performance = faster reports Clean code = easier maintenance Proper structure = scalable models Right techniques = accurate results  Key Goals  Accuracy Correct calculations  Performance Fast execution  Scalability Growth potential  Maintainability Easy updates Performance Impact of DAX Optimization  Optimized DAX  Reduced Overhead\n\n1 ⭐ Key Benefits  Reduces model size Measures don't consume storage space  Improves performance Calculated at query time, not refresh  Context-aware Adapts to filters and slicers  Faster refresh Less data to process during refresh  Lower memory usage Values computed when needed  Explanation  Measures calculated on query time  Calculated columns stored in model  Measures adapt to filter context  Calculated columns computed during refresh  Measure Sales Amount = SUM(Sales[SalesValue])  Calculated Column Sales[Sales Amount] = Sales[Quantity] * Sales[Price] USE MEASURES, NOT CALCULATED COLUMNS\n\n2  Modular Measures ↓ ⭐ Key Benefits  Improves readability Easier to understand complex logic  Easier debugging Isolate issues to specific measures  Reusability Use same measure in multiple calculations  Maintainability Update logic in one place  Team collaboration Easier for multiple developers  Explanation  Break complex formulas into smaller measures  Reuse measures instead of duplicating code  Create building blocks for complex calculations  Simplify maintenance and debugging process Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount]) Module 1 Total Cost = SUM(Sales[Cost]) Module 2 Total Units = SUM(Sales[Quantity]) Module 3 Profit = [Total Sales] - [Total Cost] Result  Modular Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount]) Total Cost = SUM(Sales[Cost]) Profit = [Total Sales] - [Total Cost]  Monolithic Profit = SUM(Sales[Amount]) - SUM(Sales[Cost]) KEEP DAX SIMPLE & MODULAR\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38964d74b4c92aa3\">>>\n</file>","display":false,"details":{"source":"openclaw-runtime-context"},"id":"0a551451","parentId":"8fa967aa","timestamp":"2026-05-12T17:50:41.904Z"}
